Package: ggplasmidZY
Title: All-in-One Plasmid and Bacteriophage Genome Visualization
Version: 0.1.1
Authors@R: c(
    person("Yang", "Zhong", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "yzhong005@e.ntu.edu.sg")
  )
Author: Yang Zhong [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Yang Zhong <yzhong005@e.ntu.edu.sg>
Description: An integrated toolkit for visualizing plasmid and bacteriophage
    genomes using 'ggplot2'. Combines circular and multi-line linear maps,
    annotated gene arrows, GC-content and GC-skew tracks, and nucleotide
    similarity comparison rings in a single plotting workflow. Provides
    automatic label placement and user-defined controls for labels, connector
    lines, colors, legends, and track geometry. Supports GenBank, FASTA, and
    annotation-table inputs, named palettes from 'ggsci', and an optional
    terminal-boundary marker for linear bacteriophage genomes displayed as
    circular maps. Comparison rings accept precomputed BLAST hits or run
    pairwise searches using a separately installed NCBI BLAST+ executable.
    Returns standard 'ggplot2' objects for further customization and export.
